  "term": "expectancy-value model",
  "definition": "The expectancy-value model explains choice and motivation in terms of whether a person believes they can succeed and how worthwhile the goal seems to them. In this packet, it includes expected success, the goal’s intrinsic and practical value, and psychological costs that can discourage action.",
